# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. Without this, a clone on Windows gets CRLF and
# bash fails on the shebang with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
*.sh text eol=lf
# .py/.ps1/.psm1 need the same rule: a Windows autocrlf checkout otherwise gets
# them as CRLF too, which is what plugin/crew/tests/test_approval_hook.py,
# test_completion_audit.py and test_crew_context_wrappers.py's
# `*_is_lf_only` tests assert against (committed blobs already carry 0 CR;
# this pins the checkout, not just the blob). Deliberately NOT extended to
# *.cmd/*.bat -- cmd.exe prefers CRLF, and
# plugin/crew/tests/test_crew_fixtures.py builds a deliberately-CRLF
# `xdotool.cmd` fixture, so forcing LF there would fight a real requirement
# rather than fix one.
*.py text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.psm1 text eol=lf
# .crew/verify.json: plugin/crew/tests/test_refresh_check.py's sabotage-anchor test reads it
# with newline="" and matches LF-only anchors, so an autocrlf checkout must not add CR.
.crew/verify.json text eol=lf
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify
